From f4f93b04c12b7582c33689e226c3c047ac3fe680 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 13:31:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.4.0: AI Advisor - read-only LAN MCP server (rmcpd)

Optional, off-by-default, second-factor-gated read-only Model Context
Protocol server so a user's own AI client (with the user's own API key)
can audit and explain this router's configuration and traffic. The API
key never touches the router; the daemon only ever reads and recommends.

Fencing (the one deliberate inbound-listener exception in an otherwise
listener-free build):
- rmcpd never starts from the boot path; it runs only after an explicit,
  code-gated ARM action writes /tmp/reaper_mcp/session, so every reboot
  comes up dark. It refuses to start without that session file.
- LAN-only: binds lan_ipaddr, adds a LAN-bridge iptables accept rule at
  start and tears it down on every exit; Bearer token on every request;
  self-terminates on session timeout, Disable, or repeated auth failure.
- Read-only: nine curated read tools; no write/apply tool exists.
- Secrets never leave: nvram whitelist + secret-fragment scrubber + log
  redaction as a second choke point.

Second factor (arming code): stored only as salt + PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256;
the code lives off-box. Admin session AND the code are required to arm;
rotating the code requires proving the current one, so stolen admin
access alone cannot enable the advisor. 5 failures lock arming 15 min.

Whole module gated on RTCONFIG_REAPER_MCP (declared in config/config.in;
on in owner builds, strippable for distributed images).

Files: new rmcpd/{rmcpd.c,Makefile}; router Makefile obj + rules; rc
start_rmcp/stop_rmcp + notify_rc dispatch (never boot-started); nvram
rmcp_* defaults; httpd reaper_mcp.cgi arming control plane; native
Reaper_Advisor.asp + menu + dashboard rail; version -> Reaper_v1.4.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
